        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Introducing Castor: A Secure Microkernel for LLM Agents]]></title>
            <link>https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor</link>
            <guid>https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor</guid>
            <pubDate>Fri, 06 Mar 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[LLM agents that autonomously invoke external tools are becoming ubiquitous. But the frameworks that power them — LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen — provide no security boundary between the LLM and the outside world. If an agent can call a tool, it can call it without limit. If it runs too long, it forgets its own instructions. If it hits a dangerous operation, there's no systematic way to pause and ask a human.]]></description>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>LLM agents that autonomously invoke external tools are becoming ubiquitous. But the frameworks that power them — LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen — provide no security boundary between the LLM and the outside world. If an agent can call a tool, it can call it without limit. If it runs too long, it forgets its own instructions. If it hits a dangerous operation, there's no systematic way to pause and ask a human.</p>
<p><strong>Castor is a microkernel that fixes this.</strong> It interposes a deterministic execution engine between the LLM and external tools, providing capability-based budgets, checkpoint/replay, and human-in-the-loop control in a single coherent system.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="the-problem">The Problem<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#the-problem" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to The Problem" title="Direct link to The Problem" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>We've been building LLM agents for production use and kept hitting the same three failure modes:</p>
<p><strong>Privilege abuse.</strong> An agent with file access decides to "clean up" and deletes production data. The framework has no concept of budgets — if the tool is registered, the agent can call it without restriction.</p>
<p><strong>Resource exhaustion.</strong> An agent asked to "research thoroughly" makes 3,000 API calls in an hour. There's no depletable budget, no cost tracking, no way to set spending limits.</p>
<p><strong>Context amnesia.</strong> After a long conversation, the agent forgets its own safety instructions because they've been pushed out of the context window.</p>
<p>These aren't edge cases. They're the default behavior of autonomous agents.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="the-os-analogy">The OS Analogy<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#the-os-analogy" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to The OS Analogy" title="Direct link to The OS Analogy" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>We noticed something: the relationship between an LLM and external tools is structurally identical to the relationship between a user-space process and the operating system kernel.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>OS Concept</th><th>Castor Analog</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>User/kernel space</td><td>LLM vs. execution engine</td></tr><tr><td>System calls</td><td>Tool invocations via <code>proxy.syscall()</code></td></tr><tr><td>Capabilities</td><td>Depletable budget tokens</td></tr><tr><td>Process scheduling</td><td>Checkpoint/replay with HITL</td></tr><tr><td>Virtual memory paging</td><td>Context window management</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>This isn't just a metaphor — it's a structural mapping. The trust boundary is real.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="what-castor-provides">What Castor Provides<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#what-castor-provides" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What Castor Provides" title="Direct link to What Castor Provides" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="1-capability-based-security">1. Capability-Based Security<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#1-capability-based-security" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 1. Capability-Based Security" title="Direct link to 1. Capability-Based Security" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>Tools declare what they consume. The kernel enforces budgets:</p>
<div class="language-python codeBlockContainer_Ckt0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#393A34;--prism-background-color:#f6f8fa"><div class="codeBlockContent_QJqH"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-python codeBlock_bY9V thin-scrollbar" style="color:#393A34;background-color:#f6f8fa"><code class="codeBlockLines_e6Vv"><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">from</span><span class="token plain"> castor </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">import</span><span class="token plain"> Castor</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> castor_tool</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> SyscallProxy</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain" style="display:inline-block"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token decorator annotation punctuation" style="color:#393A34">@castor_tool</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">consumes</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token string" style="color:#e3116c">"api"</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> cost_per_use</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token number" style="color:#36acaa">1.0</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">async</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">def</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">web_search</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">query</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">-</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&gt;</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token builtin">list</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">[</span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">]</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">return</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">[</span><span class="token string-interpolation string" style="color:#e3116c">f"Result for '</span><span class="token string-interpolation interpolation punctuation" style="color:#393A34">{</span><span class="token string-interpolation interpolation">query</span><span class="token string-interpolation interpolation punctuation" style="color:#393A34">}</span><span class="token string-interpolation string" style="color:#e3116c">'"</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">]</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain" style="display:inline-block"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token decorator annotation punctuation" style="color:#393A34">@castor_tool</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">consumes</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token string" style="color:#e3116c">"finance"</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> cost_per_use</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token number" style="color:#36acaa">50.0</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">             destructive</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token boolean" style="color:#36acaa">True</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> requires_hitl</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token boolean" style="color:#36acaa">True</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain"></span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">async</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">def</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token function" style="color:#d73a49">execute_trade</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">symbol</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token builtin">str</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> amount</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token builtin">float</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">-</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">&gt;</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token builtin">dict</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">    </span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain" style="display:inline-block"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">kernel </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token plain"> Castor</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">tools</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">[</span><span class="token plain">web_search</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> execute_trade</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">]</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">cp </span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token keyword" style="color:#00009f">await</span><span class="token plain"> kernel</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">.</span><span class="token plain">run</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">(</span><span class="token plain">agent</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> budgets</span><span class="token operator" style="color:#393A34">=</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">{</span><span class="token string" style="color:#e3116c">"api"</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token number" style="color:#36acaa">100.0</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">,</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token string" style="color:#e3116c">"finance"</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token number" style="color:#36acaa">5000.0</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">}</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:#393A34">)</span><br></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>When the budget runs out, the agent gets structured feedback — not a crash:</p>
<div class="language-text codeBlockContainer_Ckt0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#393A34;--prism-background-color:#f6f8fa"><div class="codeBlockContent_QJqH"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-text codeBlock_bY9V thin-scrollbar" style="color:#393A34;background-color:#f6f8fa"><code class="codeBlockLines_e6Vv"><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">"Insufficient capability 'api': need 1.0, have 0.5 remaining."</span><br></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>The LLM reads this and adjusts its plan.</p>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="2-checkpointreplay">2. Checkpoint/Replay<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#2-checkpointreplay" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 2. Checkpoint/Replay" title="Direct link to 2. Checkpoint/Replay" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>You can't pickle Python coroutines. Castor doesn't try. Instead, it records every completed tool call in a replay journal. Suspend raises an interrupt; resume replays from the top with cached responses.</p>
<div class="language-text codeBlockContainer_Ckt0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#393A34;--prism-background-color:#f6f8fa"><div class="codeBlockContent_QJqH"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-text codeBlock_bY9V thin-scrollbar" style="color:#393A34;background-color:#f6f8fa"><code class="codeBlockLines_e6Vv"><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">Run 1:</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">  web_search(...)    -&gt; executes, logs result</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">  execute_trade(...) -&gt; destructive! SuspendInterrupt raised</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">  Checkpoint saved.</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain" style="display:inline-block"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">Human approves.</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain" style="display:inline-block"></span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">Run 2 (replay):</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">  web_search(...)    -&gt; cached (instant)</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">  execute_trade(...) -&gt; HITL approved, execute live</span><br></span><span class="token-line" style="color:#393A34"><span class="token plain">  Agent completes.</span><br></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>This single mechanism gives us HITL, crash recovery, and preemption — all for free.</p>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="3-human-in-the-loop">3. Human-in-the-Loop<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#3-human-in-the-loop" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 3. Human-in-the-Loop" title="Direct link to 3. Human-in-the-Loop" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>Dangerous tools suspend for human review. Humans can:</p>
<ul>
<li class=""><strong>Approve</strong> — execute the tool as requested</li>
<li class=""><strong>Reject</strong> — cancel with feedback ("Don't delete those files")</li>
<li class=""><strong>Modify</strong> — provide guidance ("Only delete files older than 30 days")</li>
</ul>
<p>Castor never mutates the agent's arguments. On modify, the LLM receives feedback and re-plans. This preserves replay determinism.</p>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="4-preemptive-scheduling">4. Preemptive Scheduling<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#4-preemptive-scheduling" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 4. Preemptive Scheduling" title="Direct link to 4. Preemptive Scheduling" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p><code>asyncio.Task.cancel()</code> injects a <code>CancelledError</code> at the next <code>await</code> point. Since LLM streaming has an <code>await</code> at every chunk boundary, the kernel can preempt an agent at <strong>token-level granularity</strong> — typically 10-100ms. No shielded sections needed; the fast/slow path split handles double-execution risk.</p>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="5-context-window-management">5. Context Window Management<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#5-context-window-management" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 5. Context Window Management" title="Direct link to 5. Context Window Management" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>The Lodge subsystem monitors token usage, pins system prompts (never evicted), and removes stale messages via FIFO when the context window fills up. Agents can retrieve evicted memories with <code>search_memory</code>.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="framework-integration">Framework Integration<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#framework-integration" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Framework Integration" title="Direct link to Framework Integration" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Castor works standalone or as a <strong>guard layer</strong> for existing frameworks. We've built proven integrations with:</p>
<ul>
<li class=""><strong>smolagents</strong> — override <code>execute_tool_call()</code> to add budget + HITL</li>
<li class=""><strong>pydantic-ai</strong> — wrap <code>WrapperToolset.call_tool()</code> with budget + HITL</li>
</ul>
<p>Both integrations add Castor's guarantees without changing agent code.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="current-status">Current Status<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#current-status" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Current Status" title="Direct link to Current Status" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Phase 1 is complete:</p>
<ul>
<li class=""><strong>249 tests</strong>, 0 lint errors</li>
<li class="">All core requirements implemented (Dam, Stream, Lodge, Capability)</li>
<li class="">Sync + async multi-agent spawning with budget delegation</li>
<li class="">Token-level LLM preemption with proportional budget</li>
<li class="">CLI for checkpoint inspection (list, show, reject, modify)</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="whats-next">What's Next<a href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/blog/introducing-castor#whats-next" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What's Next" title="Direct link to What's Next" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p><strong>Phase 2</strong> will push hot paths to Rust via PyO3 for performance. You'll still <code>import castor</code> in Python — the Rust core will be a compiled extension module.</p>
<p>We're also exploring <strong>Constellation</strong> — distributed agent orchestration where checkpoints are the portable unit of execution across nodes.</p>
<p>Read the <a class="" href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/docs/whitepaper/">whitepaper</a> for the full technical treatment, or jump to the <a class="" href="https://substrate-lab.github.io/castor-docs/docs/getting-started/quickstart">quickstart</a> to try it yourself.</p>
<hr>
